      "result": "## Test Execution Complete ✓\n\nI have successfully executed and recorded all 15 test cases for the TableSpot restaurant reservation application.\n\n### Summary of Results:\n\n**✅ PASSED (11 tests):**\n- **FT-1**: Restaurant browsing displays all required information (name, cuisine, price, rating, location, description, features)\n- **FT-2**: Search and multi-filter functionality works correctly\n- **FT-3**: Reservation creation with complete booking confirmation\n- **FT-4**: Reservation cancellation with confirmation dialog and status tracking\n- **FT-5**: Review submission with rating, date, name, and text\n- **FT-6**: Coupon application and recording with reservations\n- **FT-7**: Date picker correctly enforces future-only dates\n- **FT-8**: Reservation modification preserves details and updates immediately\n- **CS-13**: Required field validation prevents incomplete submissions\n- **IX-14**: Modification dialog and cancellation confirmation both working\n- **IX-15**: Immediate state updates without page reload\n- **CT-16**: Reservation details display all required information and location\n\n**❌ FAILED (4 tests):**\n- **CS-10**: Review constraint NOT enforced - multiple reviews accepted without completed reservation requirement\n- **CS-11**: Coupon eligibility constraint NOT enforced with user feedback - ineligible coupon silently rejected without error message\n- **CT-17**: Rating and review count inconsistency - list view (4.8) vs detail view (4.5) after reviews submitted; list not updated\n\n### Key Findings:\nThe core reservation and review functionality works well, but business rule constraints lack proper validation and user feedback. The most critical issue is the rating/review count inconsistency between views, which could confuse users about a restaurant's actual quality.",
